snp3.10:11.1 starts: Next to nothing is the bad throw
snp3.10:11.2 starts: when one loses money at dice.
snp3.10:11.3 starts: But great is the bad throw
snp3.10:11.4 starts: when one gets angered
snp3.10:11.5 starts: at those well-gone.
snp3.11:1.1 starts: Asita the seer, in his mid-day meditation,
snp3.11:1.2 starts: saw the Group of Thirty—
snp3.11:1.3 starts: exultant, ecstatic—
snp3.11:1.4 starts: holding up banners, cheering wildly,
snp3.11:8.1 starts: The Sakyans then showed
snp3.11:8.2 starts: like gold aglow,
snp3.11:8.3 starts: burnished by a most skillful smith
snp3.11:8.4 starts: blazing with glory, flawless in color.
snp3.11:19.1 starts: Instructed by the one
snp3.11:19.2 starts: seeing in the future the utmost purity,
snp3.11:19.3 starts: Nālaka, who had laid up a store of
snp3.11:19.4 starts: awaited the Victor expectantly,
snp3.11:20.1 starts: On hearing word of the Victor’s
snp3.11:20.2 starts: he saw
snp3.11:20.3 starts: he asked the foremost sage
snp3.11:20.4 starts: now that Asita’s forecast
snp3.11:41.1 starts: On hearing the fame of the enlightened
snp3.11:41.2 starts: —those who practice jhāna,
snp3.11:41.3 starts: my disciple should foster
snp3.11:41.4 starts: all the more
snp3.12:5.1 starts: “Those who don’t discern stress,
snp3.12:5.2 starts: what brings stress into play,
snp3.12:5.3 starts: & where it totally stops,
snp3.12:5.4 starts: without trace;
snp3.12:5.5 starts: who don’t know the path,
snp3.12:5.6 starts: the way to the stilling of stress:
snp3.12:7.1 starts: But those who discern stress,
snp3.12:7.2 starts: what brings stress into play,
snp3.12:7.3 starts: & where it totally stops,
snp3.12:7.4 starts: without trace;
snp3.12:7.5 starts: who discern the path,
snp3.12:7.6 starts: the way to the stilling of stress:
